PROJECT: Cardano

## System Architecture

Architecture: Dual-layer blockchain architecture comprising Cardano Settlement Layer (CSL) for value transfer and staking, and Cardano Computation Layer (CCL) for smart contract execution (HIGH) [Cardano Architecture, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture]
Layer 1: Cardano Mainnet (CSL + CCL integrated via Hard Fork Combinator) (HIGH) [Cardano Architecture, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture]
Layer 2: Hydra (Isomorphic State Channels) — off-chain scaling protocol with on-chain settlement guarantees (HIGH) [Hydra Docs, https://hydra.family/]
Layer 2: Mithril — stake-based threshold multi-signature protocol for fast sync and light client bootstrap (HIGH) [Mithril Network, https://mithril.network/]
Partner Chain: Midnight — privacy-preserving partner chain built on Polkadot SDK with ZK-proofs, interoperable with Cardano mainnet via bridge design (HIGH) [Midnight Network, https://midnight.network/]
Cross-chain Messaging: Planned via Midnight bridge and sidechain infrastructure (CIP-1694 governance actions for parameter changes) (MEDIUM) [CIP-1694, https://cips.cardano.org/cips/cip1694/]
Oracle Network: Charli3 (decentralized oracle network), Orcfax (fact-based oracle) — both native to Cardano (HIGH) [Charli3, https://charli3.io/; Orcfax, https://orcfax.io/]
Bridge: Native token bridge designs for Midnight and partner chains; no canonical Ethereum bridge operated by core entities (MEDIUM) [Midnight Docs, https://docs.midnight.network/]
Appchain: Partner chain model (Midnight) allows sovereign chains with shared security via Cardano stake pool operators (HIGH) [Midnight Announcement, https://iohk.io/en/blog/posts/2022/11/18/introducing-midnight/]

## Core Components

Component: Cardano Settlement Layer (CSL)
Function: Handles ADA transfers, staking delegation, stake pool registration, native asset (multi-asset) minting/burning, and consensus via Ouroboros
Status: Live (since 2017-09-29)
Sources: (HIGH) [Cardano Architecture, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture]

Component: Cardano Computation Layer (CCL)
Function: Executes Plutus smart contracts (eUTXO model), processes Marlowe financial contracts, manages script validation and datum/redeemer logic
Status: Live (since Alonzo hard fork 2021-09-12)
Sources: (HIGH) [Plutus Docs, https://docs.cardano.org/plutus/]

Component: Ouroboros Consensus Protocol Family
Function: Proof-of-Stake consensus with formal security proofs; variants: Classic, BFT, Praos, Genesis, Chronos, Leios, Peras
Status: Live (Praos since Shelley 2020-07-29; Leios/Peras in research/prototype)
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG Research Ouroboros, https://iohk.io/en/research/library/]

Component: Plutus Platform
Function: Smart contract platform — Plutus Core (on-chain), Plutus Tx (Haskell DSL), Plutus Application Framework (off-chain), Plutus Scripts (validator scripts)
Status: Live (Plutus V1 since Alonzo; Plutus V2 since Vasil 2022-09-22; Plutus V3 in development)
Sources: (HIGH) [Plutus Platform, https://plutus.iohkdev.io/]

Component: Marlowe
Function: Domain-Specific Language for financial contracts; runs on Plutus; DSL with visual editor (Marlowe Playground) and runtime
Status: Live (mainnet 2022)
Sources: (HIGH) [Marlowe Docs, https://docs.cardano.org/marlowe/]

Component: Hydra Head Protocol
Function: Isomorphic state channels for off-chain transaction processing with on-chain settlement; multi-party heads, contestation period, fan-out
Status: Mainnet beta (2024-12 incremental releases)
Sources: (HIGH) [Hydra Docs, https://hydra.family/]

Component: Mithril
Function: Stake-based threshold multi-signature for certified snapshots; enables fast node sync, light clients, and DA governance tally verification
Status: Live mainnet (2023-02)
Sources: (HIGH) [Mithril Network, https://mithril.network/]

Component: Midnight Partner Chain
Function: Privacy-preserving smart contracts via ZK-SNARKs (Compact language), DUST token consensus, interoperability with Cardano via bridge
Status: Devnet v1 / Public testnet (2024-10)
Sources: (HIGH) [Midnight Network, https://midnight.network/]

Component: Atala PRISM
Function: Decentralized Identity (DID) and Verifiable Credentials platform (W3C standards); enterprise/government identity solutions
Status: Live mainnet (2021-04)
Sources: (HIGH) [Atala PRISM, https://atalaprism.io/]

Component: Project Catalyst
Function: On-chain governance and treasury funding mechanism; voting via stake delegation to DReps; proposal submission and assessment
Status: Live (Fund 1 2020-08; ongoing Funds 1-12+)
Sources: (HIGH) [Project Catalyst, https://cardano.ideascale.com/]

Component: Hard Fork Combinator
Function: Mechanism for seamless protocol upgrades without chain splits; combines ledger rules from multiple eras into single blockchain
Status: Live (used for all era transitions: Byron→Shelley→Allegra→Mary→Alonzo→Babbage→Conway→Chang)
Sources: (HIGH) [Cardano Consensus, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture/consensus/]

Component: Native Asset Ledger (Multi-Asset)
Function: Native token support (fungible & NFT) without smart contracts; policy IDs, asset names, minting policies, metadata (CIP-25, CIP-68)
Status: Live (since Mary hard fork 2021-03-01)
Sources: (HIGH) [Native Tokens Docs, https://docs.cardano.org/native-tokens/]

## Consensus Mechanism

Mechanism: Ouroboros Proof-of-Stake (family of protocols)
Variant: Ouroboros Praos (current mainnet since Shelley 2020-07-29) — semi-synchronous, adaptive security, stake-based leader election via VRF
Variant: Ouroboros Genesis — enables bootstrapping from genesis without trusted checkpoint
Variant: Ouroboros Chronos — clock synchronization assumptions
Variant: Ouroboros Leios — upcoming throughput-optimized design (pipelined block production, parallel validation)
Variant: Ouroboros Peras — fast finality gadget (2024 research)
Leader Election: Verifiable Random Function (VRF) — stake-proportional, private, unpredictable
Slot Duration: 1 second
Epoch Duration: 5 days (432,000 slots)
Security Model: Formal proofs in UC model / simulation-based; adaptive corruption; honest majority of stake assumed
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG Research Ouroboros, https://iohk.io/en/research/library/; Cardano Consensus, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture/consensus/]

## Execution Environment

Environment: eUTXO (Extended Unspent Transaction Output) model — not EVM, not WASM, not Move VM
Smart Contract Language: Plutus Core (typed lambda calculus, based on System F) — compiled from Plutus Tx (Haskell EDSL) or alternative languages (Aiken, Plutarch, Helios)
Transaction Validation: Two-phase — Phase 1: UTxO consumption/production rules + value preservation; Phase 2: Script execution (Plutus Core interpreter) with cost model (CPU/memory units)
Data Availability: On-chain (datum attached to UTxO, reference scripts via CIP-33 inline datums)
Deterministic Fees: Fee = a * size(tx) + b * execution_units + c * script_size (parameters governed on-chain)
Sources: (HIGH) [Plutus Docs, https://docs.cardano.org/plutus/; Cardano Architecture, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture]

## Programming Languages

Language: Haskell — core protocol, consensus, ledger, Plutus Core compiler, node implementation (GHC)
Language: Plutus Tx — Haskell-embedded DSL for writing on-chain validators (compiled to Plutus Core)
Language: Plutus Core — on-chain untyped/typed lambda calculus (System F variant)
Language: Marlowe — DSL for financial contracts (Haskell-embedded, visual editor)
Language: Aiken — ML-inspired language compiling to Plutus Core (community, production-ready)
Language: Plutarch — Haskell-embedded Plutus Core compiler (alternative to Plutus Tx)
Language: Helios — JavaScript-like language compiling to Plutus Core (browser-based IDE)
Language: TypeScript/JavaScript — off-chain tooling (MeshJS, Lucid, Cardano Serialization Lib)
Language: Rust — some tooling (e.g., cardano-node components, Mithril signer/aggregator partially)
Language: Python — some analytics/tooling (PyCardano, cardano-cli wrappers)
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG GitHub, https://github.com/input-output-hk; Plutus Platform, https://plutus.iohkdev.io/; Aiken Lang, https://aiken-lang.org/; Helios, https://helios-lang.io/]

## Development Framework

SDK: Cardano Node (Haskell) — full node implementation, CLI, submission API
SDK: Cardano CLI — transaction building, signing, submission, query, governance actions
SDK: MeshJS — TypeScript framework for dApp development (wallet connection, tx building, Plutus interaction)
SDK: Lucid — TypeScript/Deno library for transaction building and off-chain code
SDK: Aiken — Language + toolchain (compiler, LSP, package manager, testing framework) for Plutus Core
SDK: Plutarch — Haskell library for writing Plutus Core directly with type-level guarantees
SDK: Helios — Browser-based IDE + compiler for Plutus Core (JS-like syntax)
SDK: Cardano Serialization Library (CSL) — Rust/WASM/JS bindings for low-level transaction serialization
SDK: Blockfrost API — REST/WebSocket API for on-chain data (UTxO, stakes, scripts, metadata)
SDK: Koios API — Community REST API for high-performance on-chain queries
SDK: Ogmios — WebSocket JSON-RPC interface to cardano-node for local transaction submission
SDK: Kupo — Lightweight chain indexer for UTxO pattern matching (SQLite backend)
Sources: (HIGH) [Developers Portal, https://developers.cardano.org/; MeshJS, https://meshjs.dev/; Aiken, https://aiken-lang.org/; Blockfrost, https://blockfrost.io/; Koios, https://koios.rest/]

## Security Model

Validator Set: Stake Pool Operators (SPOs) — ~3,000+ registered pools; active block producers determined by stake delegation and VRF
Consensus Security: Ouroboros Praos — adaptive security under honest majority stake assumption; formal proofs in Universal Composability framework
Transaction Validation: Deterministic script validation via Plutus Core interpreter; cost model limits (CPU/memory) prevent DoS
Script Integrity: Reference scripts (CIP-33) and inline datums (CIP-32) reduce attack surface; script hash in UTxO address binds logic immutably
Light Client Security: Mithril — stake-based threshold multi-signatures for certified state snapshots; security reduces to honest stake majority
Governance Security: CIP-1694 — Constitutional Committee (threshold multi-sig), DRep delegation, SPO voting; governance actions require constitutional compliance
Network Security: P2P gossip protocol (Diffusion/Pipelining via CIP-31); peer selection via ledger peer snapshots
Cryptography: Ed25519 (keys), VRF (leader election), Blake2b-256 (hashing), BLS12-381 (Midnight ZK)
Formal Verification: Protocol specs in Agda/Coq; properties proven (chain growth, chain quality, common prefix)
Sources: (HIGH) [IOG Research Library, https://iohk.io/en/research/library/; Cardano Consensus, https://docs.cardano.org/architecture/consensus/; Mithril Network, https://mithril.network/; CIP-1694, https://cips.cardano.org/cips/cip1694/]

