## Summary

Architecture: Dual-layer (CSL + CCL) Layer 1 with Hard Fork Combinator; Layer 2: Hydra (state channels), Mithril (threshold signatures); Partner Chain: Midnight (ZK privacy)
Core Components: 12 (CSL, CCL, Ouroboros family, Plutus, Marlowe, Hydra, Mithril, Midnight, PRISM, Catalyst, Hard Fork Combinator, Native Asset Ledger)
Audit Count: 7 documented audits (Tweag, Quarkslab x2, KPMG, Trail of Bits, academic peer review x2, Mithril audit)
Major Upgrade Count: 10 major hard forks/era transitions (Byron, Shelley, Allegra, Mary, Alonzo, Babbage, Vasil, Chang/Conway, plus Mithril activation, Hydra beta)

## Open Threads

- Ouroboros Leios / Peras deployment timeline: research papers published (2023-2024) but no mainnet activation date announced; prototype implementation status unclear
- Midnight mainnet launch date: devnet v1 live 2024-10; mainnet target "2025" per communications but no firm date; bridge security model not finalized
- Plutus V3 features: referenced in CIP-1694 governance context (cost model changes, new builtins) but specification not published in CIP repository as of 2024-12
- Hydra Head multi-party liveness requirements: documentation states all parties must be online; alternative "Hydra Tail" or asynchronous designs in research but not implemented
- Mithril signer/aggregator decentralization: currently IOG-operated aggregators; roadmap for community-run aggregators not dated
- Sidechain/partner chain framework generalization: Midnight is first; CIP for generic partner chain consensus (CIP-1694 governance action for sidechain parameters) exists but no second partner chain announced
- Formal verification of Plutus Core compiler: Tweag audit 2021 covered interpreter; compiler correctness (Plutus Tx → Plutus Core) not fully verified
- Node implementation diversity: cardano-node (Haskell) is sole production implementation; no independent client (Rust/Go) at parity — single-client risk
- eUTXO concurrency solutions standardization: multiple patterns exist (batching, multiple UTxOs, off-chain sequencers, CIP-68 reference NFTs) but no canonical best practice CIP adopted
- Governance action execution latency: constitutional review period + enactment delay adds minimum ~5-10 epochs for parameter changes; impact on emergency fixes unknown